<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50976" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vindĕlĭci</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a German people</i>, <i>whose chief town was Augusta Vindelicorum</i>, the
			mod. <i>Augsburg</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 20,
				24, § 133</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 2,
			17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 4, 4, 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 14,
			8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 21</span></i>; Serv. ap. <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 1,
				243</span></i>. —Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vindĕlĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Vindelici</i>, <i>Vindelician</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					9, 85, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saltus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. B. Get. 365</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spolia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 415</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vindĕ-lĭcĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>the country of the
				Vindelici</i>, <i>Vindelicia</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 488</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
